{"annotationDigest":"sha256:a66fb7b67d10657c3fd0900c739f5241dec0dc3e61215e544346cf9117b48e56","annotationId":"rann-e17f44c8796cf943dfa47596987cdcef","author":{"agent":"claude-code","kind":"ai","model":"claude-opus-5.5"},"createdAt":"2026-10-04T08:52:50Z","disclaimer":"AI-generated review opinion derived from the evidence package. It is not a verdict, does not change readiness, and must be confirmed by a human reviewer.","disclosureCheck":{"blocking":13,"contradictions":[],"disclosures":16,"nextDecision":"human_judgement","readiness":"not_assessed"},"findings":[{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-261004-H41S"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"Before, filterEmojis kept every emoji whose keywords contain the search text anywhere, in the order of emojis.json. The picker selects the first result and Enter hands it to omarchy-menu-emoji-insert, so ok picked the broken heart (ok inside broken), tea the face with tears of joy and fr the cold face (freezing). The upstream commit 1f764b03 ranks each match with matchRank (EmojiSearch.js:35; the best place the text shows) into a whole-word, keyword-start or inside group as it reads the file. isWordChar (EmojiSearch.js:27) ends a word at anything that is not a digit, an apostrophe or a character with a case, so curly quotes, _ - and : end a word while é and ’ do not. filterEmojis returns the groups joined and cut at the limit (EmojiSearch.js:71); a fractional limit now rounds up explicitly (EmojiSearch.js:54), which keeps the old result for a fractional limit. H41S is proof work stating that order; the executable lines are the upstream ones.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":35},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":27},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":54},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":71},{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-H41S","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Emoji search now ranks whole-keyword matches first, then keyword starts, then matches inside a word (SW-REQ-261004-H41S)","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-H41S","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-261004-H41S is in review.changes (added, matchLevel function).","status":"confirmed"}},{"claim":{"params":{"requirement":"SW-REQ-261004-JATY"},"type":"requirement_affected"},"detail":"The baseline traces parseEmojis, normalizedQuery, keywordText and filterEmojis to JATY; this change rewrites filterEmojis, so the package lists JATY as code_changed with a function-level match and restamps its trace review. JATY leaves the order out of scope, and the set is unchanged: matchRank returns -1 exactly when indexOf finds no match, and 0 for an empty search text, so an emoji is listed only when it has an emoji, its keywords contain the trimmed, lowercased text and fewer than the limit come before it in the picker's (now ranked) order. Its witness test/shell.d/menu-emoji-picker-test.sh passes on this head (20 ok, re-run for this review; it also passes on the baseline code), the upstream test emojis-test.sh now verifies it too, and the package records JATY's claim as observed_pass (3 passed, 0 failed).","refs":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-JATY","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-emoji-picker-test.sh","kind":"test"},{"id":"test/shell.d/emojis-test.sh","kind":"test"},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":65},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":71}],"severity":"info","title":"SW-REQ-261004-JATY (which emojis the search lists) is a changed requirement here, and it still holds on this head","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-JATY","kind":"requirement"}],"method":"review.changes (spec, code-trace, function and call-level requirement impact)","note":"SW-REQ-261004-JATY is in review.changes (code_changed, matchLevel function).","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"Test results are ingested and current: 59 tests, 59 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped. Both changed requirements are observed passing (H41S: 20 passed; JATY: 3 passed). The upstream test test/shell.d/emojis-test.sh, which the change extends, checks the three groups, the limit after ranking, separators, curly quotes, accents, apostrophes, digits, the fractional limit and the first emoji for ok, key, tea, fr and ear on the real emojis.json; it is now run by the audit's plugins-shell command and passed (19 ok). It fails on the baseline code at 'ranks whole keywords, then keyword starts, then matches inside a word' (re-run for this review), and the known issue's evidence records known_issue_not_reproduced on Linux with the same test file. The proof-side witness test/shell.d/menu-emoji-search-bdiff-test.sh (menu-shell suite) asserts all 16 emoji inputs through the harness and golden per-group emojis. EmojiSearch.js is not a code-MC/DC target, so diffCoverage measures 0 changed decisions there, and the package maps no test to the changed code (exercisesChangedCode is unset).","refs":[{"id":"tests_pass","kind":"check"},{"id":"code_mcdc_coverage","kind":"check"},{"id":"test/shell.d/emojis-test.sh","kind":"test"},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-emoji-search-bdiff-test.sh","kind":"test"},{"id":"test/shell.d/emojis-test.sh","kind":"file","line":131},{"id":"proof/evidence/ki-menu-emoji-search-inside-word.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-H41S","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Is the fix verified? By executed tests and the behaviour comparison; code-level MC/DC does not cover EmojiSearch.js","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"test/bdiff/harness.mjs runs each revision's real picker functions from Emojis.qml (open, loadEmojis, setFilter, rebuildDisplay, activateIndex,