l/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":71},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/Emojis.qml","kind":"file","line":75},{"id":"test/bdiff/corpus/lifecycle/seq-emoji-letter.events","kind":"test"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-H41S","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: is a single-letter search allowed to change which 1000 emojis show?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Grid contents for a one-letter search\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js:filterEmojis"],"scenario":"in a live Quickshell session, open the emoji picker, type ok and press Enter: the insert helper receives the OK hand"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The harness runs the real Emojis.qml functions under node:vm, not Qt; its Enter step copies the QML key handler (Emojis.qml:219). The known issue records a check in the real shell on the base (Enter picked the broken heart for ok, the face with tears of joy for tea, the cold face for fr). No live-shell run at this head is in the package.","refs":[{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":71},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/Emojis.qml","kind":"file","line":219},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-EMOJI-SEARCH-INSIDE-WORD.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-H41S","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"low","title":"Question: does the live picker show the same first emoji as the harness?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"Live picker: type ok, Enter, read the clipboard the insert helper serves\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"detail":"The four mcdc:ignore:defensive lines of test/shell.d/menu-emoji-picker-test.sh (baseline, reviewed under REVIEW-261004-TD57) argue from the base code: out.push inside the empty-or-contains test, and a break that stops the list at the limit. This change removes out.push; matches past the limit are now pushed into the keyword-start and inside groups and cut by slice (EmojiSearch.js:71), and the loop breaks only when the whole-word group is full (EmojiSearch.js:68). The exempted combinations stay infeasible (the witness passes), but the stated reasons no longer match the code; re-reviewing them against this head would keep the exemption record accurate. mcdc_ignore_classified passed.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-emoji-picker-test.sh","kind":"file","line":8},{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-emoji-picker-test.sh","kind":"file","line":9},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":68},{"id":"shell/plugins/emojis/EmojiSearch.js","kind":"file","line":71},{"id":"SW-REQ-261004-JATY","kind":"requirement"},{"id":"mcdc_ignore_classified","kind":"check"}],"severity":"low","title":"Opinion: the JATY witness's reviewed MC/DC exemptions describe the old filterEmojis","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"H41S and JATY each inherit error_handling from SYS-REQ-260922-6642, which asks action scripts for their side effect or a loud, exit-coded refusal. The emoji search runs no script and refuses nothing: when emojis.json does not parse, parseEmojis gives an empty list and the picker shows no emojis, silently. So no test carries an error_handling tag, and each requirement records an obligation suppression with that reason (JATY's in the baseline, H41S's in this change). The package still counts both cells as not_linked, so this disclosure stays and is not cleared by this review. The loud refusal belongs to bin/omarchy-menu-emoji-insert, which this change does not touch.","refs":[{